# Community mod standard (RAD)

When creating or editing a mod under `mods/`, follow this contract. The schema is
vendored read-only at `.github/workflows/scripts/mod.schema.json` (canonical
source: `researchanddesire/dev-docs`) — do not hand-edit it.

## Folder layout (exact)

```
mods/<product>/<author>/<mod_name>/
├── cad/        # STEP required; native (F3D, etc.) optional
├── print/      # STL / 3MF (Git LFS) — optional
├── img/        # at least one image — required
├── docs/       # optional extras (BOM, PDF)
├── mod.yml     # metadata — required
└── README.md   # required
```

- `<product>` ∈ `lockbox | dtt | ossm | radr`. No spaces in names. No deeper nesting.

## mod.yml fields

| Key             | Type        | Required | Notes |
| --------------- | ----------- | -------- | ----- |
| `title`         | string      | yes      | |
| `author`        | string      | yes      | GitHub username; must match the folder |
| `product`       | enum        | yes      | `lockbox` `dtt` `ossm` `radr` |
| `description`   | string      | yes      | |
| `mod_version`   | integer ≥ 1 | yes      | bump on changes |
| `compatibility` | list        | yes      | non-empty; only tested models/revs |
| `images`        | list        | yes      | non-empty; relative paths that exist |
| `safety`        | object      | yes      | `affects_restraint_release`, `affects_applied_force`, `affects_electrical` (booleans) + `notes` |

There is **no `license` key** — license is fixed (below).

## License (fixed — not contributor choice)

- Hardware / printable (`cad/`, `print/`) → **CERN-OHL-S v2**
- Software / firmware (any code) → **MPL 2.0**
- Docs / images → **CERN-OHL-S v2**

Never add a per-mod `LICENSE` file. The root `LICENSE` path-map governs.

## Safety

Intimate devices — fill the `safety` block honestly. Anything touching
restraint-release, applied force, or electrical/charging gets a human safety
review before merge.

## Validation

`mod-lint` is the gate: `python .github/workflows/scripts/mod_lint.py`. Green = good.
